    "README.md": "# HARZ Vault v0.1 — Sovereign Storage Protocol

Content-addressed durable storage. Zero dependencies, pure Node stdlib.
Runs on a plain Node (Node 1 / Termux included) with NO Cloudflare account.

Governing law (Rabiu, 2026-10-09): the durable record is the truth.
A document is not safely stored because an ingestion request succeeded.

## Files

1. `vault.js` — protocol core: put (fsync + atomic rename + manifest fsync, THEN ack),
   get (hash-verified, hard failure on mismatch), verify / verifyAll (durable verify log),
   honest states (LIVE / CACHED / OFFLINE / STALE), capacity law (real free bytes,
   honest refusal), restart recovery (state replayed from manifest, never assumed).
2. `export-corpus.js` — resumable sovereign export job. Pulls the D1 corpus through the
   corpus worker's `/api/export` pipe into the local vault. Kill it at any point; rerun
   resumes from the durable cursor with no gaps and no duplicates.
3. `tests/run-tests.js` — acceptance suite T1–T10 (death tests). All 10 pass (see receipt).
4. `tests/sample-d1.json` — frozen 50-doc parity sample from harz-million-corpus
   (ids 1 to 1,030,814, every 21,037th doc) used by T10.

## Node 1 runbook (Termux)

1. Requirements: Node 18+ (`pkg install nodejs` in Termux). No npm install needed.
2. Copy this folder to Node 1.
3. Run the acceptance suite first:
   `node tests/run-tests.js` — expect `RESULT: 10 passed, 0 failed`.
4. Export the corpus (full run needs ~8GB+ free; the job refuses honestly if space runs out):
   `export HARZ_WAVE_KEY='<the wave key goes here, on Node 1 only, never in any chat>'`
   `node export-corpus.js https://harz-million-corpus.harz.workers.dev ./vault-root`
5. Interruption is safe: power loss, kill, offline — rerun the same command to resume.
6. Offline reading works by design: the vault core has no network path at all.

## Status laws

LIVE = hash verified this session. CACHED = stored, not re-verified now.
OFFLINE = served locally, no network verification available. STALE = freshness unguaranteed.
Cached is never presented as live. Integrity mismatch = HARD FAILURE, never wrong content.

## Scope (v0.1)

Single-node durable protocol, proven. Multi-node replication (3 verified copies) is
deliberately deferred to v0.2 until this core passes on real hardware (Node 1).
Stage 3 corpus migration only starts after: suite passes on Node 1, owner approves,
and the migration plan keeps D1 originals untouched (reversible, resumable).
